Subject: Cantor Runtime, Process Procedure, and FPGA Seven-Fold Exhaustion

Description: Seven constraint-held opposite-edge probes over runtime, procedure, shared inference, and optional hardware realization.

@ [exhaustion_uuid] bb76dca4-33af-468f-b3c6-a20a44315aee
@ [constraint_ledger] C:\Project\Cantor\narrative\research\Cantor_Runtime_Procedure_FPGA_Constraint_Ledger_2026-08-05.sop
@ [pruning_growth] C:\Project\Cantor\narrative\research\Cantor_Runtime_Procedure_FPGA_Pruning_Growth_2026-08-05.sop

& [Fold_1_AuthorityEdge] probes proposal through irreversible effect
  + expansion finds nine distinct procedure phases and five distinct hardware authorities
  + opposite edge is model-authored source reaching device or external effect
  + pruning removes every implicit authority inheritance
  + [gain_delta] exact receipts, principals, versions, and invalidation for each phase

& [Fold_2_TimeAndReplayEdge] probes one logical step through missed recurrence and crash reentry
  + expansion finds logical, fixture civil, valid, transaction, and physical cycle time must remain distinct
  + opposite edge is a replay after timeout, cancellation, or crash
  + pruning removes system clock, sleep, background timer, and timestamp causality
  + [gain_delta] explicit clock input, horizon, transition, residual, and replay boundaries

& [Fold_3_SharedInferenceEdge] probes one proposal through distributed disagreement
  + expansion finds named participants, typed messages, frame generation, causal predecessors, objections, qualifications, passes, and expiry
  + opposite edge is missing or adversarial participant during an apparently stable token cycle
  + pruning removes silence-as-assent, majority-as-truth, and shared-hidden-state language
  + [gain_delta] exact participant-set equality and generation reset semantics

& [Fold_4_GeneratedProcedureEdge] probes harmless helper through malicious or unbounded candidate
  + expansion finds schema widening, SOP-anchor substitution, covert input access, nontermination, resource exhaustion, self-invocation, and catalogue drift
  + opposite edge is a compiled candidate attempting self-admission or hidden effect
  + pruning removes ambient capabilities and direct execution after compile
  + [gain_delta] effectless sandbox, static and invocation bounds, and lifecycle refusals

& [Fold_5_CompilerCorrespondenceEdge] probes source normalization through false checked status
  + expansion finds canonical source, types, IR, diagnostics, source map, effects, costs, independent rear review, and unknowns
  + opposite edge is target self-certification with missing diff categories
  + pruning removes one-pass self-evidence and general compiler claims
  + [gain_delta] independent correspondence receipts and exact invalidation surface

& [Fold_6_HardwareEdge] probes portable IR through device loading
  + expansion finds kernel profiling, eligibility, interface, FIFO behavior, scheduling, simulation, synthesis, timing, resources, bitstream identity, signing, rollback, and side channels
  + opposite edge is model-generated hardware loaded into a device
  + pruning removes target selection and all executable hardware authority
  + [gain_delta] signed non-executable target contract plus mandatory future target addendum

& [Fold_7_OperationalEdge] probes successful fixture through migration and revocation
  + expansion finds version axes for source, schemas, IR, compiler, verifier, policy, SOP anchors, catalogue, invocation, and backend
  + opposite edge is replay after a dependency is revoked or migrated
  + pruning removes name-based compatibility and history deletion
  + [gain_delta] exact-version default, explicit migration, preserved audit, and safe residual

& [CrossFoldConvergence] reaches phase lock candidate
  + all folds converge on immutable typed state, explicit identities, bounded transitions, separate authority receipts, normalized semantic traces, and fail-closed versions
  + runtime and procedure experiment converge at forms and IR but retain distinct implementation authorities
  + hardware converges as a correspondence target rather than a semantic or present execution layer
  + no fold supports live effects, direct hidden-state sharing, arbitrary model code, or current FPGA implementation

& [ExhaustionState] is phase_locked_for_canonical_authoring
  + [fold_count] is 7
  + [hard_constraint_failure_count] is 0
  + [remaining_growth] is deferred syntax, providers, persistence, distribution, profiling, and target-specific hardware
  + [termination_reason] further current folds repeat the same identity, authority, bound, and correspondence structure without material specification gain
